HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1e5ec359, "\302\2474.19: the compiler calls this function for you, so it is checked against the header the way your own call would be \342\200\224 and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5ec2a9e9, "` is not what a string is");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2abeb16e, "name the function that frees THIS string \342\200\224 `free` for `strdup`, `sqlite3_free` for SQLite's own \342\200\224 or drop the `owned` mark and free it yourself");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_ccf254, " the header's `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6c1001b, "` \342\200\224 clang read the header, ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_70e61340, "\302\2474.19: a parameter is declared as what the header says. `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5150ddd1, "` has no name in this language \342\200\224 if it is a struct, declare it as a `record` inside this same `extern` group and the header owns its layout");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4b36102a, "\302\2474.19: a result may be wider than C's, and a parameter is declared at the header's own width and sign. Declare it `");
